3. test_max_correct | requirement: Maximum fun value is sum of all ids from 1 to n, achieved when all people are touched. | technique: Boundary value: check maximum output value. | oracle: Maximum value in output must equal n*(n+1)//2. | validity: No fun value can exceed sum of all ids; that sum is achievable when gcd(k,n)=1.
4. test_sorted | requirement: Output must be in increasing order. | technique: Output shape: check strict increase. | oracle: Consecutive output values must be strictly increasing. | validity: Specification explicitly requires increasing order.
5. test_all_integers | requirement: Output consists of space-separated integers. | technique: Output shape: check that all tokens are positive integers. | oracle: Each token must represent a positive integer. | validity: Specification requires printing integers; fun values are sums of positive ids.
6. test_output_size_bounded_by_divisors | requirement: Number of distinct fun values is at most number of divisors of n. | technique: Decision rule: compare output size to divisor count. | oracle: len(output) ≤ number of divisors of n. | validity: Each fun value corresponds to a divisor d = gcd(k,n); different d may coincide, so size ≤ divisor count.
7. test_prime_n | requirement: For prime n, only divisors are 1 and n, yielding exactly two fun values: 1 and n*(n+1)/2. | technique: Direct oracle for equivalence class of prime n. | oracle: Output must equal [1, n*(n+1)//2]. | validity: Derived from general formula applied to prime n.
