3. test_output_upper_bound_n_plus_m | requirement: Removing all spells certainly allows a path, so answer ≤ n+m. | technique: boundary value. | oracle: output > n+m. | validity: True for all inputs.
4. test_if_m_zero_then_zero | requirement: If there are no horizontal spells, the rook can go straight up from (1,1) to row 10^9 without removing any spells. | technique: equivalence partition (m=0). | oracle: output ≠ 0 when m=0. | validity: Vertical spells do not block vertical movement within the same column.
5. test_if_no_horizontal_covers_column1_then_zero | requirement: If no horizontal spell covers column 1, the rook can go straight up in column 1 without removing any spells. | technique: decision rule. | oracle: output ≠ 0 when no horizontal spell has x1 ≤ 1 ≤ x2. | validity: Vertical spells do not affect vertical movement in column 1.
6. test_output_at_most_H | requirement: Removing all horizontal spells that cover column 1 allows a vertical path in column 1, so answer ≤ H where H is the number of such spells. | technique: output bound. | oracle: output > H. | validity: Removing those H spells yields a clear column.
7. test_output_at_most_n_plus_H | requirement: Removing all vertical spells and all horizontal spells covering column 1 certainly allows a path (e.g., go right if needed then up), so answer ≤ n+H. | technique: output bound. | oracle: output > n+H. | validity: True.
8. test_output_at_least_full_width_horizontal_count | requirement: Any horizontal spell that spans the entire board (x1=1, x2=10^9) blocks all columns at its row and must be removed. | technique: output bound. | oracle: output < count of such spells. | validity: Each such spell blocks every possible vertical path at its row.
